s 'hello' can be used in a wider range of social contexts."}], "collocations": ["say hello", "hello there", "hello everyone", "hello and welcome", "wave hello", "hello again"], "translations": {"formal": "آداب عرض ہے", "primary": "ہیلو", "colloquial": "ہاں جی", "alternatives": ["سلام", "آداب", "خوش آمدید", "نمستے"], "primary_roman": "Hello", "alternatives_roman": ["Salaam", "Aadaab", "Khush Aamdeed", "Namaste"]}, "definition_en": "Used as a greeting when meeting someone, or when answering the telephone.", "definition_ur": "کسی سے ملتے وقت یا فون اٹھاتے وقت استعمال ہونے والا کلمۂ آداب یا سلام۔"}, {"pos": "noun", "antonyms": {"en": ["farewell", "goodbye", "parting"], "ur": ["خدا حافظ", "الوداع", "رخصتی"], "ur_roman": ["Khuda Hafiz", "Alwida", "Rukhsati"]}, "examples": [{"en": "She gave a warm hello to all the guests at the party.", "ur": "اس نے پارٹی میں تمام مہمانوں کو گرمجوشی سے سلام کیا۔", "roman": "Us ne party mein tamaam mehmano ko garramjoshi se salaam kiya."}, {"en": "A simple hello can make someone's day better.", "ur": "ایک سادہ سا سلام کسی کا دن بہتر بنا سکتا ہے۔", "roman": "Ek saada sa salaam kisi ka din behtar bana sakta hai."}, {"en": "They exchanged hellos before sitting down for the meeting.", "ur": "وہ میٹنگ کے لیے بیٹھنے سے پہلے آپس میں سلام و دعا کرتے رہے۔", "roman": "Woh meeting ke liye baithne se pehle aapas mein salaam o dua karte rahe."}], "register": "informal", "synonyms": {"en": ["greeting", "salutation", "welcome", "acknowledgment"], "ur": ["سلام", "آداب", "تحیہ", "خیر مقدم"], "ur_roman": ["Salaam", "Aadaab", "Tahiyya", "Khair Maqdam"]}, "confusables": [{"word": "greeting", "difference": "'Greeting' is a broader noun that encompasses any form of welcome or acknowledgment, while 'hello' as a noun specifically refers to the utterance of that particular word."}], "collocations": ["a warm hello", "exchange hellos", "a quick hello", "a cheerful hello"], "translations": {"formal": "کلمۂ آداب", "primary": "سلام", "colloquial": "ہیلو", "alternatives": ["آداب", "مرحبا", "ہیلو"], "primary_roman": "Salaam", "alternatives_roman": ["Aadaab", "Marhaba", "Hello"]}, "definition_en": "An instance or act of saying 'hello'; a greeting.", "definition_ur": "سلام یا آداب کہنے کا عمل؛ ملتے وقت کیا جانے والا کلمۂ خیر مقدم۔"}, {"pos": "verb", "antonyms": {"en": ["bid farewell", "say goodbye", "ignore"], "ur": ["الوداع کہنا", "خدا حافظ کہنا", "نظرانداز کرنا"], "ur_roman": ["Alwida kehna", "Khuda Hafiz kehna", "Nazar andaaz karna"]}, "examples": [{"en": "He helloed her from across the street.", "ur": "اس نے سڑک کے اس پار سے اسے ہیلو کہا۔", "roman": "Us ne sarak ke us paar se use hello kaha."}, {"en": "She went around the office helloing all her colleagues.", "ur": "وہ دفتر میں گھوم گھوم کر تمام ساتھیوں کو ہیلو کرتی رہی۔", "roman": "Woh daftar mein ghoom ghoom kar tamaam saathiyon ko hello karti rahi."}, {"en": "Stop helloing everyone and come sit with us.", "ur": "سب کو ہیلو کرنا بند کرو اور ہمارے ساتھ آ کر بیٹھو۔", "roman": "Sab ko hello karna band karo aur hamare saath aa kar baitho."}], "register": "informal", "synonyms": {"en": ["greet", "welcome", "salute", "acknowledge"], "ur": ["سلام کرنا", "خوش آمدید کہنا", "تسلیم کرنا"], "ur_roman": ["Salaam karna", "Khush aamdeed kehna", "Tasleem karna"]}, "confusables": [{"word": "hail", "difference": "'Hail' as a verb means to greet enthusiastically or to signal, and is more formal or dramatic than 'hello'."}], "collocations": ["hello someone", "helloing strangers", "hello the crowd"], "translations": {"formal": "تحیہ پیش کرنا", "primary": "سلام کرنا", "colloquial": "ہیلو بولنا", "alternatives": ["ہیلو کہنا", "آداب کہنا", "خیر مقدم کرنا"], "primary_roman": "Salaam karna", "alternatives_roman": ["Hello kehna", "Aadaab kehna", "Khair maqdam karna"]}, "definition_en": "To say or call out 'hello'; to greet someone.", "definition_ur": "کسی کو ہیلو کہنا یا سلام کرنا۔"}], "phonetic": {"ipa": "/həˈloʊ/", "stress": "second syllable", "syllables": "hel-lo"}, "etymology": {"history": "The word 'hello' is relatively modern, popularized in the 1800s. It is derived from 'hullo' or 'hallo', which were variants of 'hollo', used to hail ferrymen. Thomas Edison is widely credited with popularizing 'hello' as a telephone greeting in 1877, whereas Alexander Graham Bell preferred 'ahoy'. The word quickly became the standard English greeting worldwide.", "origin_word": "hāl + Old High German 'halâ / holâ'", "origin_meaning": "A shout used to hail a ferryman; an exclamation to attract attention", "first_known_use": "1826", "origin_language": "Old English / Germanic"}, "memory_tip": {"mnemonic": "Think of 'HELLO' as an acronym: 'Happiness Everyone Loves Loving Others' — it reminds you that a hello spreads happiness and love.", "visual_association": "Imagine a bright sunny morning where two friends spot each other across a park and wave enthusiastically, their mouths open saying 'HELLO!' with big smiles on their faces."}, "urdu_poetry": {"poet": "Unknown", "source": "Unverified", "couplet_ur": "سلام اس پر جو دیتا ہے سلام اجنبی کو بھی\\nمحبت کا یہی اندازِ عام ہوتا ہے", "ai_generated": true, "couplet_roman": "Salaam us par jo deta hai salaam ajnabi ko bhi\\nMohabbat ka yahi andaaz-e-aam hota hai", "translation_en": "Blessed is the one who greets even a stranger with a hello;\\nThis is the common and beautiful way of love."}, "word_family": [{"ur": "ہیلو / سلام", "pos": "exclamation / noun / verb", "word": "hello"}, {"ur": "ہیلو کہا", "pos": "verb (past tense)", "word": "helloed"}, {"ur": "ہیلو کہتے ہوئے", "pos": "verb (present participle)", "word": "helloing"}, {"ur": "سلام / ہیلوز", "pos": "noun (plural)", "word": "hellos"}], "urdu_proverb": {"proverb_ur": "سلام میں پہل کرنا بڑائی کی نشانی ہے۔", "proverb_roman": "Salaam mein pehel karna barayi ki nishani hai.", "translation_en": "Being the first to greet is a sign of greatness and nobility."}, "related_words": {"see_also": ["hi", "hey", "greet", "salutation", "goodbye", "farewell", "welcome"], "thematic_group": ["hi", "h