hukm", "fatwa"]}, "confusables": [{"word": "verdict", "difference": "'Verdict' is specifically a decision made in a legal or judicial context by a jury or judge, whereas 'decision' is broadly applicable to any choice or conclusion in any context."}, {"word": "choice", "difference": "'Choice' refers to the act of selecting from several options, while 'decision' emphasizes the process of deliberation and commitment to a final conclusion."}, {"word": "resolution", "difference": "'Resolution' often implies a firm commitment or formal declaration (e.g., a New Year's resolution or a UN resolution), while 'decision' is a more general term for any concluded judgment."}], "collocations": ["make a decision", "reach a decision", "final decision", "tough decision", "unanimous decision", "split decision", "wise decision", "hasty decision", "informed decision", "life-changing decision", "decision-making", "reverse a decision"], "translations": {"formal": "فیصلہ", "primary": "فیصلہ", "colloquial": "فیصلہ", "alternatives": ["قرارداد", "حکم", "نتیجہ", "عزم"], "primary_roman": "faisla", "alternatives_roman": ["qarar-daad", "hukm", "nateeja", "azm"]}, "definition_en": "A conclusion or resolution reached after careful thought or deliberation; the act of making up one's mind about something.", "definition_ur": "کسی معاملے میں سوچ بچار کے بعد کوئی نتیجہ یا قرارداد تک پہنچنا؛ ذہن کو کسی بات پر مستحکم کرنے کا عمل۔"}, {"pos": "noun", "antonyms": {"en": ["indecisiveness", "wavering", "irresolution", "hesitancy"], "ur": ["ڈانواں ڈول پن", "تذبذب", "کمزوری", "بے ارادگی"], "ur_roman": ["danwan dol pan", "tazabzub", "kamzori", "be-iradagi"]}, "examples": [{"en": "A great leader must act with decision and clarity, especially in times of crisis.", "ur": "ایک عظیم رہنما کو خاص طور پر بحران کے وقت فیصلہ کن پن اور وضاحت کے ساتھ عمل کرنا چاہیے۔", "roman": "Ek azeem rahnuma ko khas tor par bohran ke waqt faisla-kun pan aur wazahat ke saath amal karna chahiye."}, {"en": "His decision in handling the crisis earned him great respect from his team.", "ur": "بحران سے نمٹنے میں اس کے فیصلہ کن پن نے اسے اپنی ٹیم سے بہت عزت دلائی۔", "roman": "Bohran se nipatne mein us ke faisla-kun pan ne use apni team se bahut izzat dilai."}, {"en": "She is known for her decision and never wavers once she has made up her mind.", "ur": "وہ اپنے فیصلہ کن پن کے لیے مشہور ہے اور ایک بار ذہن بنا لینے کے بعد کبھی نہیں ڈگمگاتی۔", "roman": "Woh apne faisla-kun pan ke liye mashhoor hai aur ek baar zehan bana lene ke baad kabhi nahin dagmagati."}], "register": "formal", "synonyms": {"en": ["decisiveness", "determination", "resolve", "firmness", "resoluteness"], "ur": ["عزم", "پختہ ارادہ", "ثابت قدمی", "استقلال"], "ur_roman": ["azm", "pukhta irada", "sabit-qadami", "istiqal"]}, "confusables": [{"word": "decisiveness", "difference": "When 'decision' is used to mean the quality of being decisive, it is near-synonymous with 'decisiveness'. However, 'decisiveness' is exclusively used for this quality, while 'decision' primarily refers to a specific choice or conclusion."}], "collocations": ["act with decision", "a man of decision", "show decision", "lack of decision"], "translations": {"formal": "قوتِ فیصلہ", "primary": "فیصلہ کن پن", "colloquial": "فیصلہ کن پن", "alternatives": ["عزم و ہمت", "پختگی", "ثابت قدمی"], "primary_roman": "faisla-kun pan", "alternatives_roman": ["azm-o-himmat", "pukhtagee", "sabit-qadami"]}, "definition_en": "The quality of being able to make choices quickly and confidently; decisiveness.", "definition_ur": "جلدی اور اعتماد کے ساتھ انتخاب کرنے کی صلاحیت؛ فیصلہ کن پن۔"}], "phonetic": {"ipa": "/dɪˈsɪʒ.ən/", "stress": "second syllable", "syllables": "de-ci-sion"}, "etymology": {"history": "The word entered English in the early 15th century via Old French 'décision', derived from Latin 'decisio', from 'decidere' meaning 'to cut off' or 'to determine'. The root 'de-' (off) + 'caedere' (to cut) metaphorically conveys the idea of 'cutting off' all other options to arrive at a conclusion.", "origin_word": "decisio", "origin_meaning": "a cutting off, settlement, from decidere — to cut off, decide", "first_known_use": "15th century", "origin_language": "Latin"}, "memory_tip": {"mnemonic": "Think of 'decision' as 'de-cision' — like scissors (cision sounds like scissors) cutting through confusion. When you make a decision, you cut through all the options and choose one, just like scissors cut through paper.", "visual_association": "Picture a pair of large golden scissors cutting through a tangle of knotted ropes, each rope labeled with a different option. Once the scissors cut, one clear, straight path is revealed — that is your decision."}, "urdu_poetry": {"poet": "Unknown", "source": "Unverified", "couplet_ur": "فیصلہ کر لے تو پھر ڈر کچھ نہیں رہتا\\nجو راہ چن لے مسافر، سفر کٹ ہی جاتا ہے", "ai_generated": true, "couplet_roman": "Faisla kar le to phir dar kuch nahin rehta\\nJo raah chun le musafir, safar kat hi jaata hai", "translation_en": "Once a decision is made, no fear remains;\\nThe traveler who chooses a path will complete the journey."}, "word_family": [{"ur": "فیصلہ کرنا", "pos": "verb", "word": "decide"}, {"ur": "فیصلہ کن", "pos": "adjective", "word": "decisive"}, {"ur": "فیصلہ کن طور پر", "pos": "adverb", "word": "decisively"}, {"ur": "تذبذب", "pos": "noun", "word": "indecision"}, {"ur": "غیر فیصلہ کن", "pos": "adjective", "word": "indecisive"}, {"ur": "فیصلہ کن پن", "pos": "noun", "word": "decisiveness"}, {"ur": "فیصلہ ساز", "pos": "noun", "word": "decision-maker"}, {"ur": "فیصلہ سازی", "pos": "noun", "word": "decision-making"}], "urdu_proverb": {"proverb_ur": "جو فیصلہ کرے وہی آگے بڑھے", "proverb_roman": "Jo faisla kare wohi aage badhe", "translation_en": "Only those who make decisions move forward."}, "related_words": {"see_also": ["verdict", "judgment", "conclusion", "resolution", "choice", "determination"], "thematic_group": ["debate", "deliberation", "consensus", "vote", "referendum", "opinion", "stance", "policy"]}, "script_varian